    "scenesThatPass": [
      "TIMLIN: What is the relationship between you two?\nCAPRICE: I remove these tumours as part of our performance. We are performance artists. We perform together.\nTIMLIN: And you are qualified to perform surgery?",
      "CAPRICE: If consent is legally given, there's really no issue there.\nTIMLIN: I'm speaking of your professional relationship. You wouldn't want to kill your performance partner, would you?",
      "TIMLIN: I'm sorry. It's forbidden to record in here.\nCAPRICE: I was thinking we could use it for our performance. We record the most intimate things.\nTIMLIN: I'm sorry, but it's illegal. This department does not yet exist.",
      "CAPRICE: Too bad.\nTIMLIN: Did you do this, Caprice? This is your work?\nCAPRICE: The tattooing, you mean? Yes. It's been part of our act for years.\nCAPRICE: Decorating and celebrating the inner body and so on. From a practical point of view, it makes it easier to identify the new organ under the …",
      "BERST: The Sark autopsy module was one of the best units we ever made. It's gorgeous.\nROUTER: They're legendary.\nBERST: So complex."
